From dc75c0e2d7c7e9a5eb4335e38989863a6764b657 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James <james@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:18:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] SmartPort and FujiNet cards; full-screen fixes; safer
 slot saves

New cards, sharing one firmware and one 6502-facing core
(src/apple2/peripherals/smartport):

- SmartPort: a SmartPort controller with two hard disks and two UniDisk
  3.5 drives, from ProDOS-order images (.po .hdv .2mg, MacBinary, inside
  .zip/.gz read-only). Drives 1-2 answer the hard disk commands, so the
  hard disk keys (Shift+F3/F4) and Harddisk Image keys serve it; F3/F4
  put a 400K/800K image in the 3.5 drive of that number, and the 3.5
  drives keep their images under 'SmartPort 3.5 Image 1/2'.
- FujiNet: the units of a FujiNet-PC (Apple build) over TCP with the
  FujiNet project's SmartPort-over-SLIP protocol, as AppleWin's
  SmartPortOverSlip card does. Section [FujiNet]: Listen Address, Port
  (1985), Response Timeout, Boot Wait.

The firmware moves every reply into memory with 6502 stores, so the card
never writes behind the bank switching, and needs no CPU registers.

Also:
- read 'Screen Width'/'Screen Height' from linapple.conf;
- hide the pointer and treat the window as full screen when started so;
- sync() after a save slot is written or erased.

